        | other | not connected (16-31, 52-59, 76-82, 88, 93-95) |

        <!-- overview:begin -->

        ### Diagrams

        ![Logic block diagram](assets/diagrams/hi3520dv300-logic.svg)

        ![Register blocks by function](assets/diagrams/hi3520dv300-blocks.svg)

        ![Boot flow](assets/diagrams/hi3520dv300-boot.svg)

        ### Variants (data sheet chapter 1)

        One data sheet covers the Hi3521A and the Hi3520D V300: one address map, one set of register blocks. The chips differ as follows.

        | | Hi3521A | Hi3520D V300 |
        |---|---|---|
        | CPU | Cortex-A7, up to 1.1 GHz, NEON and FPU | Cortex-A7, up to 800 MHz, NEON and FPU |
        | Caches | 32 KB L1 I + 32 KB L1 D, 128 KB L2 | same |
        | DDR | one 32-bit DDR3/DDR3L controller, up to 800 MHz, up to 512 MB | one 16-bit DDR3/DDR3L controller, up to 800 MHz, up to 512 MB (brief data sheet) |
        | SATA | 2 x SATA 3.0 | 2 x SATA 2.0 |
        | H.264 | enc 4x1080p@30 + 4xCIF@30 + dec 1x1080p@30; dec 5x1080p@30 or 10x720p@30 | enc 4x720p@30 + 4xCIF@30 + dec 4x720p@30; dec 2x1080p@30 or 4x720p@30 |
        | Video input (VI) | four 8-bit or two 16-bit ports (up to 16xD1/960H, 16x720p, 8x1080p TDM) | two 8-bit or one 16-bit port (up to 8xD1/960H, 8x720p, 4x1080p TDM) |
        | Package | TFBGA, 19 x 19 mm, 0.8 mm pitch | Epad-LQFP256, 28 x 28 mm, 0.4 mm pitch |
        | Supplies | core 1.1 V, CPU 1.25 V, I/O 3.3 V, DDR 1.5 V; 3 W typical | core and CPU 1.15 V, I/O 3.3 V, DDR 1.5 V; 2.5 W typical |
        | Common | H.264 baseline/main/high decode L4.2 and encode L5.1, MJPEG/JPEG, IVE, HDMI 1.4 + VGA + CVBS (1080p@60), one HD and one SD graphics layer plus a 128x128 cursor, 3 unidirectional I2S/PCM, integrated audio codec, 1 gigabit Ethernet (RGMII/RMII/MII, TSO), 2 USB 2.0 host, 3 UART, 1 SPI (2 CS), IR, I2C, GPIO, SPI NOR/NAND (1/2/4 bit, 2 CS), 4 KB BOOTROM + 16 KB SRAM, AES/DES/3DES, RTC | |

        ### Boot (data sheet 1.3)

        * BOOTROM_SEL (pin MDCK) = 1: boot from the BOOTROM, which starts the serial download mechanism (HiTool); if the serial link times out the chip boots from the external SPI NAND/NOR flash.
        * BOOTROM_SEL = 0: boot from the external SPI NOR/NAND flash (SFC).

